A||||8||Slammed Fiero||The misfortune of a mustang ...Poem||||1||
Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||09-02-2001||02:13 PM||||My poem for a mid 90's GT mustang that I had some altercations with<P><BR>You went out tonight , and thought you were fast.<P>Then a 4700lbs grocery getter handed you your ass.<P>Light after light you tried and tried , with little idea of what lurked inside<P>Your wheels shined up , your tips polished bright , you were sure you had no equal that night.<P>Don't worry you say as you approach the light , a Big Caprice wagon is the only thing in sight.<P>You laugh and giggle at the woodgrain on it's side , still with no clue as to the monster inside<P>The light goes green , the beast awakes , your in for trouble but it's too late<P>The mighty LT1 grumbes and roars , the race is over and you got yours.<P>Things are not always as they seem.<BR>By the 3rd and final race the guy rolled down his window and was furious , said he wasn't trying , why am I racing a wagon anyway ..Blah Blah Blah.<P>He got me off the line everytime by about 1/2 a car length , the problem here is the gear in the wagon is a 2.8? and it take a min to get the 17" ROH wheels with 255/50's spinning. Hit around 25mph and pulled hard on him about a car length every time.<P><BR>Why do people get mad when a station wagon beats them , or any car for that matter?? I beat a kid last week in a nice lookin precidia , all done up with a body kit and wheels , next light he said it was the coolest station wagon he had ever seen , really nice guy.<P>Some people's kids...sheesh<P>JM<P>86 GT <BR>94 Caprice wagon , lowered , 3" duals right from the motor,  Dynomax ultra flows , Eibach springs , Police sway bars , 255/50/17's all around on 9" rims , Revalved tranny and shift servo's. LT1 260hp stock , head work , ASM cold air induction bigger TB , all sorts of little goodies.<P>The only choice when it comes to driving fast and blending in..||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||09-02-2001||02:36 PM||||Some peoples kids?! Man, you writing POEMS about beating a car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||09-02-2001||04:28 PM||||Yeah well I'm bored , waiting for paint on calipers and rotor hats to dry so I can put my 11.25" discs together.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||09-02-2001||06:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>writing POEMS about beating a car.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Hey, what's wrong with that? <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008648.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008648.html</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||09-02-2001||08:15 PM||||I have to agree. If you get beat, take it like a man (or woman, as necessary).  Hell, I'll race almost anything.  My feeling is, I might win, but if I don't, I wanna see what your car can do.  When I was 17, I was driving a '71 Mercury Marquis (big car) with a 429 Police Interceptor engine.  Of course, since I was 17, I was the fastest thing around.  I picked on a Vette one night, only to find out when he floored it that it was a 69 427 Six-Pack!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>My car was running awesome and screaming for all she was worth.  And he left me like the Millennium Falcon hitting Hyperdrive....  I'm doing 90 and he literally drove out of my sight in seconds.  I haven't had my door blown off that bad before or since.  When I caught up to him later, I thanked him for the experience.  To me, it was a privledge to see a car that fast do what it was built to do.<P>To this day, the sound of those end carbs opening up still stick in my memory.  MAN, what an awesome car!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>But then there was the time I raced a Maserti Merak SS.  We were running side by side - pretty evenly matched, and he was grinning cuz he hear my engine starting to wind out.  Then about 100mph I hit 3rd gear and pulled away from him.  Broke his little heart.  But in his defense, he pulled onto some twisties and proceeded to show me what a Maserti can do.  We both proved our points that night.||||reg||14
Z||000005||FieroLisa||09-03-2001||02:11 AM||||awww Jonathan you wrote a POEM how sweeet!!! hehehe just kidding, out playin with your dad's wagon and kickin some @ss? You drive that thing like a d@mn psycho   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Go be unbored now!!!!<P><BR>PS hmm someone has my shifter knob and my car is gettin kindly lonely without the nice new short shifter...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by FieroLisa (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||09-04-2001||02:50 AM||||Hehehehe thanks man, I love it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The Impalla SS has to be one of the best 'sleepers' and your aftermarket one with the wood sides is just great.  Reminds me of a friend of my dad's who had a Vw Beatle with a 454 big block in it (no joke, went right up to the front seats, rears were of course gone.)  He ate vettes all the time, what a scary and hillarious sight! I hear he tried to turn once, but the understeer kept it going in a straight line.<P>And it's all true, except the line part. heh.<P>I dunno why people get mad, but hey, post-1970s mustang drivers :S)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
